# EKS Cluster Setup & Kubernetes Networking

## 1. EKS Cluster Setup

EKS cluster create karte time mainly ye cheezein decide karte hain:

* Kubernetes version
* Region
* VPC/Subnets
* Node Groups
* Instance types
* On-Demand / Spot capacity
* IAM roles
* Add-ons

> **Note:** Kubernetes/EKS version aur pricing frequently change hoti hai, isliye exact support status AWS documentation se verify karna chahiye.

---

## 2. Terraform

Terraform se EKS ke supporting infrastructure ko automate kar sakte hain.

Example:

```text
Terraform
   ↓
VPC
Subnets
IAM
Security Groups
EC2 / Bastion
EKS Resources
```

Jump/Bastion server ke liye small EC2 instance use kiya ja sakta hai.

---

## 3. EKS Access

### Local Machine

```text
Laptop
  ↓
AWS Authentication
  ↓
EKS API Server
```

### Bastion / Jump Server

```text
Admin
  ↓
Bastion Server
  ↓
EKS API Server
```

Bastion centralized access aur security controls ke liye useful ho sakta hai.

> Production mein direct internet exposure ke bajay private access/VPN/SSM jaise controlled access patterns prefer kiye ja sakte hain.

---

## 4. AWS CLI & Kubeconfig

AWS credentials configure:

```bash
aws configure
```

EKS kubeconfig generate/update:

```bash
aws eks update-kubeconfig \
  --region <region> \
  --name <cluster-name>
```

Then:

```bash
kubectl get nodes
```

Kubeconfig mein cluster endpoint, CA information aur authentication configuration hoti hai.

