# 5. Kubernetes Service Types

## ClusterIP

Default Service type.

```text
Pod → Service → Pod
```

Internal cluster communication ke liye.

---

## NodePort

Node ke specific port par Service expose karta hai.

```text
Client
  ↓
NodeIP:NodePort
  ↓
Service
  ↓
Pods
```

Mostly testing/simple use cases ke liye.

---

## LoadBalancer

Cloud provider ke through external Load Balancer provision kar sakta hai.

```text
Internet
   ↓
AWS Load Balancer
   ↓
Service
   ↓
Pods
```

---

## ExternalName

Service ko external DNS name se map karta hai.

Example:

```text
Application
    ↓
ExternalName Service
    ↓
External Database
```

---

# 6. ALB vs NLB

| Feature        | ALB              | NLB                      |
| -------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------ |
| Layer          | L7               | L4                       |
| Main Protocols | HTTP/HTTPS       | TCP/UDP/TLS              |
| Routing        | Host/Path based  | IP/Port based            |
| Use Case       | Web applications | High-performance TCP/UDP |

### ALB Example

```text
example.com/api
       ↓
Backend Service

example.com/frontend
       ↓
Frontend Service
```

### NLB

Low-latency, high-throughput Layer-4 workloads ke liye useful.

---

# 7. Ingress

**Ingress Service type nahi hai.**

Ingress ek Kubernetes API resource hai jo external HTTP/HTTPS traffic ko Services tak route karta hai.

Example:

```text
Internet
   ↓
Load Balancer
   ↓
Ingress
   ├── /api → Backend Service
   └── /web → Frontend Service
```

Ingress commonly provide karta hai:

* Path-based routing
* Host-based routing
* TLS termination

Ingress ko actual traffic handle karne ke liye **Ingress Controller** chahiye.

---

# 8. Namespaces

Namespace cluster ke andar logical separation provide karta hai.

Common namespaces:

```text
default
kube-system
kube-public
kube-node-lease
```

Example:

```text
Cluster
 ├── dev
 ├── qa
 ├── staging
 └── prod
```

Useful for:

* Team separation
* Resource organization
* RBAC
* ResourceQuota

`kubens` namespace switch karne ke liye convenient CLI tool hai.

---

# 9. Workload Controllers

### Deployment

Stateless applications ke liye.

```text
Deployment
    ↓
ReplicaSet
    ↓
Pods
```

### StatefulSet

Stateful applications ke liye.

Features:

* Stable Pod identity
* Stable network identity
* Ordered deployment/scaling

Example:

```text
db-0
db-1
db-2
```

### DaemonSet

Selected/every eligible node par Pod run karta hai.

Common use:

* Monitoring
* Logging
* Networking agents

### Job

Finite task ko completion tak run karta hai.

```text
Job → Pod → Complete
```

### CronJob

Scheduled Jobs run karta hai.

```text
CronJob
   ↓
Job
   ↓
Pod
```

